.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH sinteractive 1  "sinteractive 1.0.0-dev" 
.SH NAME
sinteractive \- Persistent interactive sessions on Slurm compute nodes
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsinteractive\fR [\fB\-\-node\fR] [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-partition\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-time\fR] [\fB\-j\fR|\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-mem\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-mouse\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR] [\fB\-\-detach\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Persistent interactive sessions on Slurm compute nodes
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-node\fR \fI<NODE>\fR
Request a specific compute node (`\-\-nodelist`)
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-partition\fR \fI<PART>\fR
Slurm partition
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-time\fR \fI<TIME>\fR
Wall time (`8h`, `30m`, `1d12h`, or Slurm `D\-HH:MM:SS`)
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<N>\fR
Number of CPUs (`\-\-cpus\-per\-task`)
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-mem\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Memory (`\-\-mem`)
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Tag the session with a name for easy reattach
.TP
\fB\-\-mouse\fR
Enable mouse support in the session
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR
Disable mouse support (overrides `SINTERACTIVE_MOUSE`)
.TP
\fB\-\-detach\fR
Launch without attaching; print connection info and return
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable JSON output (with `\-\-detach`)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
sinteractive\-launch(1)
Launch a new session (the default when no subcommand is given)
.TP
sinteractive\-attach(1)
Reattach to a session by JOBID or NAME (your only session when omitted)
.TP
sinteractive\-ensure(1)
Reuse the session named NAME, or launch it if absent (implies \-\-detach)
.TP
sinteractive\-status(1)
Show one session\*(Aqs status
.TP
sinteractive\-refresh(1)
Re\-check a session\*(Aqs time budget now and update its cache
.TP
sinteractive\-list(1)
List running sessions
.TP
sinteractive\-cancel(1)
Cancel a session
.TP
sinteractive\-queue(1)
Your job queue: running, pending (with reasons), and recent history
.TP
sinteractive\-monitor(1)
Live CPU/GPU/process view of a session\*(Aqs node, or any host
.TP
sinteractive\-snapshot(1)
One\-shot resource sample of this host
.TP
sinteractive\-events(1)
Stream session events (NDJSON)
.TP
sinteractive\-peek(1)
Read the last lines of a session\*(Aqs screen
.TP
sinteractive\-send(1)
Type a command into a session\*(Aqs shell
.TP
sinteractive\-agent\-context(1)
Brief a coding agent on the session it is running inside
.TP
sinteractive\-quota(1)
Storage quota (Bodhi daemons; wraps curc\-quota on Alpine)
.TP
sinteractive\-hook(1)
Claude Code hook entry points
.TP
sinteractive\-statusline(1)
Claude Code statusLine command
.TP
sinteractive\-mcp(1)
MCP server over stdio
.TP
sinteractive\-install\-claude(1)
Install the Claude Code skills, hooks, statusline and MCP server
.TP
sinteractive\-doctor(1)
Check this install and, optionally, every compute node
.TP
sinteractive\-completions(1)
Print shell completions
.TP
sinteractive\-man(1)
Print the man page (roff)
.TP
sinteractive\-schema(1)
Dump the JSON schemas of the machine\-readable outputs
.TP
sinteractive\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v1.0.0\-dev
